{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468949-advice-about-running-a-uratha-campaign-in-detroit","id":468949,"title":"Advice about running a Uratha campaign in Detroit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-04T16:48:31-07:00","id":468949,"title":"Advice about running a Uratha campaign in Detroit","content":"I'm looking for tips from those who live in Detroit or like the city, documentaries, sites, books, whatever a foreigner need to know to engage his players like they're living there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1960-thelinuxlich","name":"thelinuxlich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:45:18-07:00","id":469047,"title":"","content":"This is great, I'm basing my current werewolf game in Michigan as well. It's started in Kalamazoo, at Western Michigan University with some connections over to Detroit, and possible Flint. <br /> <br /> Seriously, Michigan has so much variety, history and landscape it is a treasure trove for werewolf. Check out the upper peninsula for deep forests / backwoods. Check out the great lakes for a variety of waters, islands, beach scenery. There's small lake communities that are fabulously wealthy, urbane or even trailer park poor. You have Detroit and Flint for murder capital hardcore cityscapes, gangs, drugs, whatnot. You have the dying (maybe being reborn) auto industry, the rich and historical farming industry, the transplanted pharmeuctical companies. And you get a good dose of all four seasons, with an emphasis on nasty cold winters and sloshy wet springs. You also have a solid american indian history there. <br /> <br /> As far as specifics for living in Detroit :/ I'm pretty sure a google search will reveal tons of interesting information about the history and current situation.. Don't forget all the surrounding bedroom communities, there are there are a lot of flourishing ones just outside of Detroit. <br /> <br /> Good luck! Hope to hear about your game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:50:42-07:00","id":469054,"title":"","content":"Oh, also check out the Errol Flynns, to get a taste of how Detroit gangland was born: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errol_Flynns\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errol_Flynns</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T22:03:45-07:00","id":469174,"title":"","content":"As someone whose screwed up family on his father's side used to be a VERY big deal in Flint before the town and the family went south (my father's family were the top Ford salesmen in Flint from my great grandfather in the 30s to my grandfather's death from bone cancer in the 70s), I personally would love to play in a campaign in that area. Between the prophetic dreams and the drug dealing alone, my family history is giving me some great character ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T07:56:14-07:00","id":469338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468949-advice-about-running-a-uratha-campaign-in-detroit?p=469174#post469174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone whose screwed up family on his father's side used to be a VERY big deal in Flint before the town and the family went south (my father's family were the top Ford salesmen in Flint from my great grandfather in the 30s to my grandfather's death from bone cancer in the 70s), I personally would love to play in a campaign in that area. Between the prophetic dreams and the drug dealing alone, my family history is giving me some great character ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would love to hear your ideas - I have some (hopefully) novel ideas for Flint, but could flesh out my world with some outside wolf concepts! (I admit it: I'm shamelessly trying to outsource some world building with this request.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:16:12-07:00","id":469523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468949-advice-about-running-a-uratha-campaign-in-detroit?p=469338#post469338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would love to hear your ideas - I have some (hopefully) novel ideas for Flint, but could flesh out my world with some outside wolf concepts! (I admit it: I'm shamelessly trying to outsource some world building with this request.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The ideas ultimately come down to a family that seems like a respectable upper class family on the outside, but has some dark stuff going on behind closed doors. Including some mental illness and addiction issues on top of the stuff I already mentioned.<br /> <br /> First up, you have my dad's cousin Louie, who was the drug dealer in question. He often involved my dad in his dealing, including having my dad smuggle drugs into the boarding school where he was sent. My once dad tricked my grandmother into watering his pot plants while he was in boarding school (my grandmother didn't realize that they were pot plants). Louie ultimately died in a car crash following an argument with another member of the family (I forget exactly who), the trunk of the wrecked car was full of quaaludes (which, in case you don't know, were a seditive drug that was intended to treat insomnia, but was very popular for recerational purposes in the 70s disco scene.). Now, I'm not saying that Louie was run off the road by rival dealers while on the way to deliver those quaaludes, but it seems like it could be the case.<br /> <br /> As for the prophetic dreams, my mom and dad have a story about how before I was born, he saw the winning lottery numbers in a dream. He wakes up and asks my mom for a pen and paper so he can write them down, but my mom was all &quot;Shut up and go back to bed.&quot; So my dad tries to remember the numbers when he buys the ticket, but he can only remember the first 4 or 5 number. So he doesn't win the jackpot, but he does win about 500 bucks using the numbers he remembered seeing in the dream. And just so you guys know, my mom has no reason to lie for him, as my parents are bitterly divorced.<br /> That being said, my mom has had the occasional dream of real events that have yet to occur. The difference is that my dad's dreams predict happy events in the future and mom's dreams predict negative events (like the time she dreamed about a plane crash, woke up the next morning and turned on the news to see that a plane crash had happened over night while she was asleep.<br /> <br /> I have more stories about my dad's family in flint, but I would need to go back through my notes before I post them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T19:53:33-07:00","id":469796,"title":"","content":"WOW, didn't see that coming! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1960-thelinuxlich","name":"thelinuxlich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T20:56:09-07:00","id":469848,"title":"","content":"The point that I am trying to make is that my father's family is perfect for use as a particularly screwed up and cursed Ivory Claw bloodline in a Wod/werewolf campaign. If I were storytelling a werewolf campaign in Flint I would probably link the downfall of the family to the downfall of flint. Maybe some sort of fisher king effect where the health of the Ivory Claw family patriarch is tied to the health of the territory and the fall of the family caused the fall of Flint, or the other way around.<br /> <br /> But I am glad you guys liked this little peak into the skeletons in my family's closet. And that's just on my dad's side....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T02:24:12-07:00","id":469987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468949-advice-about-running-a-uratha-campaign-in-detroit?p=469848#post469848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point that I am trying to make is that my father's family is perfect for use as a particularly screwed up and cursed Ivory Claw bloodline in a Wod/werewolf campaign. If I were storytelling a werewolf campaign in Flint I would probably link the downfall of the family to the downfall of flint. Maybe some sort of fisher king effect where the health of the Ivory Claw family patriarch is tied to the health of the territory and the fall of the family caused the fall of Flint, or the other way around.<br /> <br /> But I am glad you guys liked this little peak into the skeletons in my family's closet. And that's just on my dad's side....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love the mention of prophetic dreams! I wonder if that could be rolled into or used as a tell for a wolf blooded? One of the plot threads in my campaign is running around an expanding drug ring as well... hmmm! Thanks for sharing the interesting stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T04:34:32-07:00","id":470053,"title":"","content":"There is an entire Let's Play for Werewolf called <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?446663-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-quot-Detroit-Rock-City-quot\" target=\"_blank\">Detroit Rock City</a>.<br /> It's technically 1E, but may provide some great ideas for running a game in Detroit!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?446663-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-quot-Detroit-Rock-City-quot\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here For Link</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T12:43:51-07:00","id":470317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468949-advice-about-running-a-uratha-campaign-in-detroit?p=469987#post469987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love the mention of prophetic dreams! I wonder if that could be rolled into or used as a tell for a wolf blooded? One of the plot threads in my campaign is running around an expanding drug ring as well... hmmm! Thanks for sharing the interesting stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do use my father's family in a campagin, then I have a few pieces of advice for portrying them.<br /> <br /> First, they are a family of car salesmen. They lie, charm, seduce and shmooze for a living and they can't turn off that behavior, even with their own family or (if you use them as Ivory Claws) their packmates. Social attributes and skills should be primary on their character sheets.<br /> <br /> Second, they are narcissists who have trouble empathizing with other people. However, they develop strong emotional connections with their pets, to the point where one of the nastiest fights in both of my father's divorces (the first being my mother, the second being my former step mother) was over custody of the pets. So, they would probably have wolf packmates.<br /> <br /> Third (which plays into the first two), the men in my father's family are very sexual people. My grandfather and father both cheated on their wives. My grandfather had a mistress who saw him in the hospital when he was dying and my father kept a list of every women he had sex with (which I assume was to feed his ego). My mother found the list when she was cleaning her stuff out of his house during the divorce. He listed most of the women by name, when he didn't know their name he gave them a a label like &quot;girl at truck-stop&quot; or &quot;black girl&quot;. Thus, I would make their inability to keep it in their pants their big weakness that PCs could take advantage of, in that I could see these Ivory Claws getting seduced by a Forsaken who fed their ego.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-06-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:41:31-07:00","id":473683,"title":"","content":"I'm a Detroit Native, most of the information in terms of statistical and historical information is easily found on the internet, however that being said I'll pass along a few tidbits.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1.) Detroit Gangs aren't really connected to the other big American Gangs. The Crips and the Bloods didn't really get a strong foothold in the area, the Native population kept them out.<br /> <br /> 2.) The City Council is often times more important than the mayor and wars often with the Mayor. Many of the Council are corrupt and rule parts of Detroit like their own personal little fiefdoms.<br /> <br /> 3.) The Auto-Industry is NOT in Detroit and hasn't been in Detroit for a long time now. The Auto-Industry is instead in the surrounding suburbs, particularly in the down river area where most of White Flight ended up going. The Auto-Industry doesn't employ anywhere near the what it once did, but is still a powerful force and it's Unions in particular are strong. The Auto-Industry allows for employment and middle class incomes for even non-college educated people, but it's harder and harder to get a job with them.<br /> <br /> 4.) Detroit's population is 90% African-American.... When you're in the city itself, most of the people you're going to run into are going to be black.<br /> <br /> 5.) Detroit is a sport's town, there are lots of Sports Bars, Tiger Stadium (Comerica Park) in the heart of Downtown is always packed when the Tigers are playing. The Redwings are also a big deal (Though more to the outside suburban population) and are widely considered to be the best team in Hockey. Detroit has the term &quot;Hockey Town&quot; Actually copyrighted. The Pistons are loved and perform well even if it's been 10 years since they won a championship...and the Lions, despite how much they suck, are beloved by Michiganders.<br /> <br /> 6.) Casinos...something the Werewolf 2nd ed book got terribly wrong, is how many Casinos are in Detroit. There are 3 alone in the city... MGM, Greektown, and the Motorcity, the MGM is the biggest.<br /> <br /> 7.) Large swaths of Detroit are completely abandoned. You can find places where you can walk for blocks where almost nobody lives. There is a severe housing crisis in the city in terms of how many are abandoned, and squatters are a real issue. A friend of mine bought some houses on the Auction House and is dealing with Drug Dealers who are squatting in his properties. The way our Squatting rules work, means it's increadibly difficult to get rid of Squatters when they take over a property, because you have to take them to Court first...and give them 90 days to vacate... They can particularly contest the evicition if they've lived in the property for over a year and have made &quot;Improvements&quot; to it.<br /> <br /> 8.) Good luck getting Police to show up in Detroit. The Department is so understaffed bodies can go for over a day before the police investigate. In the bad neighborhoods you can just expect the Police not to show up. In the case of the Drug Dealers who showed up in my buddie's property, it took several different days of calling to get Police to show up at all.<br /> <br /> 9.) Winter here can begin as early as November and go until early April. Winter is fucking miserable here. We get ridiculous snow falls in January and February in particular. Last year Most Detroit area schools were closed for an extra week due to the Snow fall, this year it was only 3 extra days before the administration decided to say &quot;Fuck it&quot; and declare this as the new normal.<br /> <br /> 10.) Due to the terrible winters and how poor our state and the Detroit area is, our roads are terrible and perpetually under construction. Constant construction begins as early as possible and goes all the way until snow fall in late November sometimes due to the massive potholes and fractures expanding ice and water in Winter create.<br /> <br /> 11.) Nearby Dearborn has the highest population and percentage of Arabic people in all of the United States. There's a part of Dearborn called little Lebanon where most of the signs are written in Arabic and you can get real good Arabic cuisine and a ton of mosques are found. Because of this, most Michiganders in the South East area don't hold as many prejudices toward Arabic people as many other Americans do because they've been in the area since the early 1900's. After 9/11 there was a fear of possible backlash happening, but it didn't.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps, just some things I can remember off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","user":"Orphan81","date":". 04-08-2015, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}